/-! # 0500: certified polynomial approximation of the smooth kernel part `Rk`

`Rk s = exp(s/2)/sinh s − 1/s`. For `0 < s ≤ log 5`, `|Rk s − Q(s/2)| ≤ 2·10⁻²⁴`, where `Q = ql` is
the degree-80 Taylor polynomial of `t ↦ Rk (2t)` (exact rationals, generated by `gen_q.py 80`).

Proof: `Rk(2t) = N/D` with `N = t cosh t + t sinh t − sinh t cosh t`, `D = 2t sinh t cosh t ≥ 2t²`;
`sinh`, `cosh` are replaced by degree-<30 truncations with `Real.exp_bound` errors; the exact
polynomial remainder and the error multipliers are bounded by coefficient absolute sums at
`a = 4024/5000 ≥ log 5 / 2`, checked by `decide +kernel`. No LeanCert; kernel-only decision procedures.
 -/

